{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/2019-05-26---Exposing-ElasticSearch-From-An-Azure-VM/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"0f78a62a-0e6b-5df8-a9a0-434452f5bffc","html":"<p>After I set up ElasticSearch on a Windows Server 2019 VM in Azure, I noticed that I could query the instance from the VM itself but not from outside of it.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/8c5dc/error.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 13.750000000000002%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/8ac56/error.webp 240w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/d3be9/error.webp 480w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/e46b2/error.webp 960w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/f992d/error.webp 1440w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/882b9/error.webp 1920w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/055f0/error.webp 2384w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/8ff5a/error.png 240w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/e85cb/error.png 480w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/d9199/error.png 960w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/07a9c/error.png 1440w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/29114/error.png 1920w,\n/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/8c5dc/error.png 2384w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/49fcd037a13c2bce29e79e11cc5a096e/d9199/error.png\"\n            alt=\"Console output\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>The solution to expose it was two-fold:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Assign <code class=\"language-text\">network.host</code></li>\n<li>Assign <code class=\"language-text\">discovery.seed_hosts</code></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Without the latter, you will find an error like this in your logs (<code class=\"language-text\">C:\\ProgramData\\Elastic\\Elasticsearch\\logs</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"text\"><pre class=\"language-text\"><code class=\"language-text\">[2019-05-26T15:55:43,504][INFO ][o.e.b.BootstrapChecks    ] [rapide] bound or publishing to a non-loopback address, enforcing bootstrap checks\n[2019-05-26T15:55:43,519][ERROR][o.e.b.Bootstrap          ] [rapide] node validation exception\n[1] bootstrap checks failed\n[1]: the default discovery settings are unsuitable for production use; at least one of [discovery.seed_hosts, discovery.seed_providers, cluster.initial_master_nodes] must be configured</code></pre></div>\n<p>These values worked for me:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"text\"><pre class=\"language-text\"><code class=\"language-text\">network.host: 0.0.0.0\ndiscovery.seed_hosts: [\"127.0.0.1\", \"[::1]\"]</code></pre></div>\n<p>I verified it worked by executing the following request. Change <code class=\"language-text\">&lt;IP></code> with <code class=\"language-text\">localhost</code> if you test on the VM or the VM’s public IP if you execute it outside of it.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"text\"><pre class=\"language-text\"><code class=\"language-text\">Invoke-WebRequest -method GET 'http://&lt;IP>:9200/_cat/indices?v'</code></pre></div>\n<p>The output should look something like this:</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/28884/output.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 43.333333333333336%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/8ac56/output.webp 240w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/d3be9/output.webp 480w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/e46b2/output.webp 960w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/f992d/output.webp 1440w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/26f96/output.webp 1755w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/8ff5a/output.png 240w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/e85cb/output.png 480w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/d9199/output.png 960w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/07a9c/output.png 1440w,\n/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/28884/output.png 1755w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/89eb8f32a4e586f88e408b0d28379350/d9199/output.png\"\n            alt=\"Console output\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>","fields":{"slug":"/posts/2019-05-26---Exposing-ElasticSearch-From-An-Azure-VM/","tagSlugs":["/tag/azure/","/tag/elastic-search/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2019-05-26T20:00:00.000Z","tags":["Azure","ElasticSearch"],"title":"Exposing ElasticSearch from an Azure VM","description":"Exposing your ElasticSearch service from an Azure VM","socialImage":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2019-05-26---Exposing-ElasticSearch-From-An-Azure-VM/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}